# 1. The recommended Alo King stack

## Product and operations

```text
Customer channel: WhatsApp
Merchant channel: dedicated merchant WhatsApp number + portal
Driver channel: driver portal/PWA or controlled web interface
Customer website: discovery, menu, tracking, support, merchant claims
Merchant portal: orders, menu, hours, campaigns, reports
Operations console: dispatch, exceptions, refunds, support, verification
```

## Backend

```text
Supabase Postgres
Supabase Auth
Supabase Storage
Supabase Realtime
Supabase Edge Functions
GitHub Actions
```

## AI

```text
Claude API: deep reasoning, difficult support, menu review, policy-sensitive workflows
OpenAI API: structured extraction, embeddings or selected model workflows where appropriate
Deterministic code: prices, permissions, status transitions, payments, dispatch, limits
```

AI must never own the business facts. It may interpret a message and choose a tool, but server code owns:

- prices;
- totals;
- menu availability;
- merchant ownership;
- order state;
- customer consent;
- payment state;
- delivery zones;
- driver assignment;
- refunds;
- permissions.

## Integrations

Use MCP where a connector safely improves development or operations:

```text
GitHub: issues, pull requests, branch context, CI results
Supabase: schema inspection, migrations, logs, read-only data checks
Meta/Kapso documentation: current WhatsApp API details
Monitoring: errors, webhook failures, latency, delivery failures
Browser: merchant portal and customer-flow testing
```

MCP is a tool connection layer, not a reason to give Claude unrestricted production access. Anthropic’s documentation describes remote HTTP/SSE and local stdio MCP servers, project-scoped configuration, and connectors from Claude.ai that can also become available in Claude Code. [4]

