# 5. Create specialist Claude Code agents

Project agents belong under `.claude/agents/`. Anthropic documents custom subagents with their own prompts, tool restrictions, permissions, model choice, skills, hooks, and memory. [3]

Create these agents:

```text
.claude/agents/
  alo-architect.md
  supabase-reviewer.md
  whatsapp-specialist.md
  merchant-ops-reviewer.md
  payment-security-reviewer.md
  ai-safety-reviewer.md
  test-engineer.md
  release-reviewer.md
```

## Recommended roles

### `alo-architect`

Read-only first. Reviews boundaries, state machines, data ownership, and migration impact.

### `supabase-reviewer`

Checks migrations, RLS, indexes, functions, triggers, foreign keys, transaction safety, and tenant isolation.

### `whatsapp-specialist`

Checks templates, 24-hour windows, webhook verification, event idempotency, message limits, retries, buttons, lists, and bilingual copy.

### `merchant-ops-reviewer`

Checks merchant acceptance SLAs, fallback notifications, substitutions, pauses, refunds, driver handoff, and operational recovery.

### `payment-security-reviewer`

Read-only review of payment links, webhooks, amount/currency validation, idempotency, refunds, ledger entries, secrets, and PII.

### `ai-safety-reviewer`

Checks prompt injection, tool authorization, model claims, hallucinated prices, allergy advice, consent, and human handoff.

### `test-engineer`

Creates tests from the behavior contract, including unhappy paths and race conditions.

### `release-reviewer`

Runs final diff, tests, migration, deployment, and rollback review.

Use read-only agents for review and editing agents only for narrowly scoped implementation. This reduces the chance that a single session changes architecture, code, data, and deployment all at once.

