# 6. MCP strategy for Alo King

## Use MCP for reading and controlled operations

Recommended connector permissions:

| Connector | Development | Staging | Production |
|---|---|---|---|
| GitHub read issues/PRs | allow | allow | allow |
| GitHub create branch/PR | allow | allow | allow with review |
| Supabase schema/read-only SQL | allow | allow | allow read-only |
| Supabase migrations | local/staging | allow | manual approval only |
| Logs/monitoring | allow | allow | allow read-only |
| Payment provider | mock/sandbox | sandbox | no automatic money actions |
| WhatsApp/Kapso send | mocked | test numbers | no autonomous bulk sends |
| Customer data export | synthetic only | restricted | prohibited by default |

## Safe `.mcp.json` principles

- Keep secrets in environment variables or the provider’s secure authentication flow.
- Do not commit API keys.
- Prefer project-scoped servers for repo development.
- Use read-only database tools by default.
- Use separate sandbox and production server names.
- Make production write tools require explicit approval.
- Test connector startup in CI and fail if a required MCP server is skipped.

Anthropic’s current headless documentation also explains that Claude Code can run with structured JSON output, restricted tools, and explicit permission modes. This is useful for safe CI reviews, but production actions should still require an approval boundary. [6]

## MCP tools Alo King should eventually have

```text
github.get_issue
 github.create_branch
 github.open_pull_request
 github.get_ci_status

supabase.read_schema
