# 7. Hooks: enforce safety automatically

Claude Code hooks run at lifecycle events and can inspect or allow/deny tool calls. Anthropic documents `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, session events, prompt-based hooks, and agent hooks. [5]

Use hooks as guardrails, not as a replacement for normal code review.

## Recommended hooks

### Pre-tool destructive-command blocker

Block or ask before:

```text
rm -rf
DROP DATABASE
TRUNCATE
supabase db reset against non-test targets
production deploy
bulk WhatsApp send
payment/refund commands
```

### Post-edit formatter and typecheck

After edits to TypeScript:

```text
prettier
eslint targeted files
tsc --noEmit, where practical
```

### Stop hook release reminder

Before Claude declares a task complete, require it to report:

```text
tests run
lint/build results
migration status
security concerns
unresolved TODOs
```

### Secret scanner

After edits, scan for:

```text
OPENAI_API_KEY
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
KAPSO secrets
webhook secrets
payment keys
JWTs
private keys
```

### Production-environment guard

The hook should detect the target environment and refuse autonomous destructive commands when:

```text
APP_ENV=production
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=production
PAYMENT_MODE=live
WHATSAPP_MODE=live
```

