# 8. GitHub workflow: one issue, one branch, one PR

## The standard loop

```text
Claude.ai product decision
→ GitHub issue with acceptance criteria
→ Claude Code plan
→ feature branch/worktree
→ implementation
→ tests
→ specialist review
→ PR
→ CI
→ human approval
→ staging
→ smoke test
→ production release
```

## Good GitHub issue template

```markdown
## Problem
[What is broken or missing?]

## User outcome
[What should the customer, merchant, driver, or operator be able to do?]

## Scope
[Included and explicitly excluded behavior]

## State transitions
[Before → after states]

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] ...
- [ ] ...

## Failure cases
- [ ] duplicate webhook
- [ ] timeout
- [ ] unauthorized actor
- [ ] provider failure
- [ ] stale data

## Data and security
[Tables, RLS, PII, secrets, audit trail]

## Tests required
[Specific tests]
```

## Claude Code prompt for an issue

```text
Read the GitHub issue and inspect the repository before editing.

Do not implement yet. First return:
1. current behavior;
2. affected files and migrations;
3. state-machine impact;
4. authorization and RLS impact;
5. notification/message impact;
6. test plan;
7. rollout and rollback plan.

Wait for my approval of the plan before changing files.
```

Once approved:

```text
Implement only the approved plan. Work on a feature branch. Add or update tests for happy paths, race conditions, duplicate webhooks, authorization failures, provider failures, and retries. Run targeted tests, lint, typecheck, and build. Do not deploy or modify production data. Open a PR summary when complete.
```

