# 9. Parallel development with worktrees

Use separate Claude Code sessions or worktrees for independent work:

```text
Worktree A: customer ordering/cart
Worktree B: merchant notifications
Worktree C: menu extraction
Worktree D: driver dispatch/tracking
Worktree E: security and RLS review
```

Do not have two agents edit the same migration or shared domain file simultaneously.

Each worktree must:

- start from a known branch;
- have a clear scope;
- run its own tests;
- commit small changes;
- merge through a PR;
- be reviewed before integration.

Claude Desktop supports isolated Git worktrees for parallel sessions and provides diff/PR review and CI monitoring capabilities. [7]

