# 13. CI and headless Claude Code

Use headless Claude Code for **review and analysis**, not autonomous irreversible business actions.

Good CI jobs:

```text
PR diff security review
PR test-plan review
migration risk review
documentation consistency check
failed-CI diagnosis
release-note generation
weekly dependency review
```

Example shape:

```bash
claude -p \
  --bare \
  --permission-mode dontAsk \
  --allowedTools Read,Grep,Glob \
  --output-format json \
  --json-schema '{"type":"object","properties":{"findings":{"type":"array"}},"required":["findings"]}' \
  "Review the current PR diff for security and data-integrity risks. Do not edit files."
```

Use `--bare` for deterministic scripts when you do not want personal hooks, local MCP servers, memory, or unrelated skills loaded. Use structured output for CI parsers. Do not place live secrets in prompts or shell history. Anthropic documents headless mode, restricted tools, structured output, and permission modes for this use. [6]

## CI safety rules

- run on a read-only checkout where possible;
- do not allow production MCP servers;
- do not auto-approve payment, deletion, migration, or broadcast tools;
- fail if a required MCP server is skipped;
- store only sanitized logs;
- pin or control tool versions;
- require human review for merge and deployment.

