# 14. What not to delegate to Claude autonomously

Do not allow a general Claude session to autonomously:

- send a mass WhatsApp campaign;
- delete customer data broadly;
- refund or transfer money;
- change production RLS;
- run a destructive migration;
- rotate production secrets without a runbook;
- change Meta/Kapso ownership;
- change payment-provider configuration;
- publish a legal or tax attestation;
- expose customer or driver personal data;
- mark an order delivered without evidence;
- accept a vendor order without merchant authorization.

Claude can prepare the change, show the exact payload, run tests, and create a PR or approval request. A human or dedicated protected workflow performs the irreversible action.

